WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.001
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.703
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.405
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:08.174
[ Cheers and applause ]
We got a full audience.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.775
I'm very excited
about the show tonight.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:11.844
Charlize Theron is here.
-Oh!

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:14.814
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.216
Willie Nelson
is also our guest tonight.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:18.852
Willie Nelson.

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:21.621
For appearing on the show,

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.289
we sent Willie
an edible arrangement.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.391
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.426
Not fruit -- it was
an arrangement of edibles.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.395
And he likes gummies.

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:30.763
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.032
Let's get to some news.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.033
Well, guys,
in a speech last night,

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:37.236
former Vice President Mike Pence
made his clearest effort yet

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.072
to distance himself from Trump

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.341 line:0%
by saying he was proud
to certify the election.

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:44.276
Wow.

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:46.279
It's a whole different side
of Pence.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.714
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.781
Next he says he wants to be

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.183
grand marshal
of the pride parade.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.852
-I mean, it's amazing
what's happening to him.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.187
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:58.091
Meanwhile, Trump can't believe
Pence turned against him.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.226
He was like, "Boy, just when
you think you know a guy

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.595
that you send an angry mob
into the Capitol building

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.630
to murder."

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.698
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.203
Pence also tried to
lighten the mood

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.737
by telling a joke,

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:14.139
and he delivered it
as only Mike Pence can.

00:01:14.139 --> 00:01:15.241
-There was this farmer

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.542
who decided to take his cow
to market.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.377
So he loaded the cow
in the truck and the dog

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:20.446
and headed into town.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.415
But on his way there,
there was a traffic accident.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.750
Cow and the truck
went in one ditch,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.819
and the farmer and dog
went in the other.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.221
They ended up in court.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.825
And the attorney for the other
driver was questioning,

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:36.028
"Isn't it true that you said you
never felt better in your life?"

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.331
He said, "Sir, would you like to
explain the circumstances

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.398
in which you made that comment?"

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:40.767
He said, "Yeah,
I reckon I would."

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.935
Me and the cow was in one ditch,

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.836
and the truck and dog
was in the other.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.039
And I seen the sheriff,
and he walked over,

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.373
he looked down at that dog.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:50.043
It had a broke back --
it wasn't going to get better.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.278
He got his revolver out and
put it next to the dog's ear,

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.279
and he shot him.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.148
And again, he mercifully
put his revolver

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:59.051
to the forehead of that cow
and pulled the trigger.

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:02.321
Then that sheriff walked over
to me and said,

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.523
"And how are you feeling?"

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.392
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.527
-Wow!

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.996
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.264
-Wow.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.533
-Wow!

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.534
The Pence was like,
"D-Darn, I told it wrong.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.102
Let me try it again
from the top.

00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:18.137
There was this farmer,

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.572
he was in a ditch."

00:02:20.572 --> 00:02:22.108
What was that joke?
Seriously.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.210
If you're looking to break up
your Fourth of July barbecue,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.311
tell that one.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.379
I mean, that's --

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.613
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:28.881
Shooting the dog?

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:30.015
-Broken back.

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:31.884
-"Pulled his revolver out
and aimed at dog."

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.153
-"He wasn't gonna get
any better."

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:35.755
-It got worse
when the camera panned out

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.390
and it was just a group of
preschool kids.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.892
And they go, "Oh."

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.560
Awful.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.528
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.930
Get this. According to
a new book coming out,

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.833
Trump made fun, apparently,
of Rudy Giuliani

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.402 line:0%
for spitting during meetings.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.670 line:0%
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.673 line:0%
And even told him
that he sucked on TV.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.107
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:57.043
Spitting, sucking, sweating,
leaking --

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.577
he's like every awful guy
at Planet Fitness

00:02:58.577 --> 00:02:59.779
rolled into one guy, you know?

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.847
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:03.283
Rudy took it all
in stride, though.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.484
He's like, "Look, he teases me,
but at the end of the day,

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:06.886
he also ruined my life."

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:10.590
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.658
Meanwhile, today,
Vice President Kamala Harris

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:15.828 line:0%
made her first visit
to the U.S./Mexico border.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:19.164
Yeah, she visited
the border town of El Paso.

00:03:19.164 --> 00:03:22.001
Is it me or "El Paso" is not
the best name for a border town?

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.002
-Yeah.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:26.438
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:27.840
-How about No Pass-O?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.009
[ Applause ]

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.712
Some business news.

00:03:33.712 --> 00:03:36.816 line:0%
Popeyes just introduced
the new "I Don't Know" meal

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:40.186 line:0%
for people who can't decide
what to order.

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:42.121
How can you be undecided

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.058
when the entire menu
has basically one thing?

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.559
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.926
It's not like
customers are thinking,

00:03:47.926 --> 00:03:51.097
"Should I have the fried
chicken or the, uh, sushi?

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.765
What do you think?

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.535
What do you think
I should have at Popeyes?"

00:03:55.535 --> 00:04:00.606
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.675
"How fresh are
the lobster tails?"

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.677
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.579
Actually, they offer
the same meal at Arby's,

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.247
only it's the cook
who has no idea what's in it.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.482
-Oh, there you go.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.851
-"I don't know.
Uh, no, hey.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.786
It's bleeding, whatever it is,
so I don't know.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.289
It's something."
-"Yes, sir."

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.357
-And get this, astronomers
have identified

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:21.327
a "extremely eccentric
mini planet"

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.995
that just entered
our solar system,

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.331
and it's on course
to pass by Earth.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.700
It's pretty exciting,
but we were curious what exactly

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.336
is an extremely
eccentric mini planet?

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.371
So here now
to talk about their trip

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:35.408
is the extremely
eccentric mini planet.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.643
♪♪

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:40.146
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.414
-[ British accent ]
Oh, my God.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.349
Jimmy, I can't believe I'm here.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.284
This is so random.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.785
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:48.854
-It's not too random.
We did invite you.

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:50.390
-Totally.
It's just that astronomers

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.125
are always telling me
I'm so eccentric.

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.292
You know, first they'll be like,

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:55.428
"Look at that normal planet
over there."

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:58.063
But then I'll be like, "Um,
I'm not like the other planets.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:01.200
I'm a semi-amateur
craft cocktail mixologist."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.035
Hello?
-Uh-huh.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:06.972
So what exactly makes you
an eccentric planet?

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.974
-Well, my taste in music
is super-eclectic.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:11.177
Like, sometimes I listen
to Lady Gaga,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:14.647
but then sometimes
I listen to, like, a podcast.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.049
It's like my mind
is on shuffle.

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.851
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.320
-And that classifies you as an
extremely eccentric planet?

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.256
-Well, technically,
it's because I'm so small.

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:25.024
Because people --
people are always telling me

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.059
"Oh my gosh, Planet,
you're so fit."

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:30.796
And I'm like, "Um, you haven't
seen me on Taco Tuesday."

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:33.298
[ Laughs ]

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:35.935
-Well, maybe you could compare
and contrast yourself

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.603
with another planet.
-Sure.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:40.606
So, like, Mars is red
and has a couple moons, right?

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.107
-Sure.
-Normal planet.

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:44.309
Whereas I collect
Funko Pop! figurines

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:47.546
and have a mustache tattoo
on my index finger.

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:50.183
Eccentric! Eccentric!
-Yeah, you're very eccentric.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:51.784
I got it. I got it.
I got it.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.152
Give me another example.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.655
-Or, like, Earth has water
and can sustain life, right?

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:58.024
-Yeah.
-Normal planet.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:02.528
Whereas I perform ukulele covers
of rap songs on Periscope.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:05.231
Extremely eccentric.

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:07.233
-One last thing. That's not --
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.769
That's not --

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:11.471
That's not your
real accent, is it?

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:12.971
-[ American accent ]
No, it's completely fake.

00:06:12.971 --> 00:06:14.073
-All right, good.
Thank you.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.242
The extremely eccentric
mini planet.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:18.177
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.079
♪♪

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.915
[ Laughs ] My gosh.

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.753
He's a-dork-ably eccentric.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:29.422
-Yeah, a-dork-ably.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.890
-And finally,
earlier this week,

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.526
police in Pennsylvania
broke up an exorcism

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.695 line:0%
in the lumber aisle
of a Home Depot.

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:37.730 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.235
Yeah, an exorcism
in the lumber aisle.

00:06:43.235 --> 00:06:46.372
Police laughed until
the 2x4 projectile vomited.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:47.840
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.309
Then they held a seance to
summon a being from far beyond,

00:06:51.309 --> 00:06:52.544
a Home Depot employee.

00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:54.379
"Does anyone work here?"

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:56.048
I want to quickly mention

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.584
the Miley Cyrus concert
on Peacock.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.586
It's out now, too.
It's awesome, by the way.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:03.089
So check it out, yeah, if you're
a fan of music in general.

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.523
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:07.359
It's on Peacock. She crushes.
We love you, Miley.

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:09.929
And I wanted to give another
shout-out to The Roots.

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.964
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.601
Look what I received.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:19.638
Look what I received today.
Oh, la, la, Sasson!

00:07:19.638 --> 00:07:21.674
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.511
-Wow.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:29.915
-You released a deluxe version
of "Do You Want More?!!!??!"

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:31.850
This is your second album.
Is this correct?

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:35.221
-Yeah, second, but our
major label debut.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.156
Our second album.
Yeah.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:41.327
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:43.462
-It comes with
a booklet in here.

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:47.866
It comes with four
super 180 gram vinyls.

00:07:47.866 --> 00:07:49.468
Look at this jam.
Come on, you don't mess around.

00:07:49.468 --> 00:07:51.236
When The Roots do something,
they do it right.

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:52.304
Look at this guy.

00:07:52.304 --> 00:07:54.340
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:01.280
I love the pictures in here.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.016
I love the stories in here.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:06.885
I want to show a picture
of Quest and Tariq.

00:08:06.885 --> 00:08:08.487
Look at these.
-Babies.

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:09.822
-Look at these kids.

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:12.124
-Aww.
-Look at these kids.

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:14.026
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:15.561
-They're like, we're going to be
on "The Tonight Show"

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.363
one day with Jimmy Fallon.

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:19.098
Yeah.

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.499
You know what I found
interesting in this

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:23.835
is the whole story
about you signing for Geffen

00:08:23.835 --> 00:08:26.204
and how Rich --
Richard was like,

00:08:26.204 --> 00:08:28.808
"Dude, I don't know.
They might drop you guys."

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:33.712
-Yeah, the last minute,
we decided to exile to the UK

00:08:33.712 --> 00:08:36.381
and live there for like four --

00:08:36.381 --> 00:08:38.184
what, three to four years
almost?

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.952
On and off, touring?
-Yeah.

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:43.655
-Was this the record that
kind of broke the band open?

00:08:43.655 --> 00:08:45.290
Like, this is --
-Yeah.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.892
Yeah. Absolutely.
-This was it?

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:48.126
-That was it.

00:08:48.126 --> 00:08:50.028
-The one after this
was "Illadelph--"

00:08:50.028 --> 00:08:51.096
-"Illadelph Halflife."

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:52.598
Yeah, and then yeah.

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:54.400
-That's my favorite,
but I'll tell you,

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.734
hey, what are you gonna do?

00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:58.938
But I love
"Do You Want More?!!!??!"

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:01.940
And the title,
is that based off the track,

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.876
which based off the Arsenio
Hall thing, or no?

00:09:04.876 --> 00:09:07.313
-Yeah, we happened to see

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:10.049
Arsenio had his version
of, like --

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:12.418
it was like Letterman's
human tricks thing?

00:09:12.418 --> 00:09:14.019
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Stupid human tricks?

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:18.924
-Yeah. Well, we saw jazz great
playing bagpipes.

00:09:18.924 --> 00:09:20.459
-Rufus Harley.
-Rufus Harley. Yeah.

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:22.361
-Yeah.
He played bagpipes?

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:23.762
-We saw him on "Arsenio Hall,"

00:09:23.762 --> 00:09:25.063
and he happened to be
in Philadelphia.

00:09:25.063 --> 00:09:26.732
So we looked him up
in the White Pages,

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:28.266
if you remember
what the White Pages were.

00:09:28.266 --> 00:09:29.534
-Yeah, of course
I remember the White Pages.

00:09:29.534 --> 00:09:31.203
-They still make
the White Pages?

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:32.604
-The White Pages, great.

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:34.040
And you found him
in the White Pages?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.274
-Yeah, we did.
-Not in the Yellow Pages.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.709
-Rufus Harley.
-Just under his name,

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:38.477
and you got him
over to the studio.

00:09:38.477 --> 00:09:39.745
-He didn't believe us.
-Were you the first --

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:41.314
-We had to have cash in hand
immediately

00:09:41.314 --> 00:09:42.915
as soon as he got to the studio.

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:46.118
-Were you the first hip-hop
group to ever have a bagpiper?

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:47.686
-Yes.
-Absolutely. Absolutely.

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:49.721
-[ Laughs ] I love it.

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:51.924
And then it turned out
to be the title.

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:54.292
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:09:54.292 --> 00:09:56.495
-Well, you know I love vinyl,
so I appreciate this.

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.297
And congrats, Roots.
This is -- Check this out.

00:09:58.297 --> 00:10:00.799
If you love music, get this.

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:04.403
"Do You Want More?!!!??!"
Deluxe Edition.

